          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பாசம் — pācam — \"family affection; attachment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தாத்தாவுக்குப் பேரன் மேல் நிறைய பாசம். tāttāvukkup pēraṉ mēl niṟaiya pācam. Grandfather is very attached to his grandson."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மேல் \"on\" marks the one loved: அவன் மேல் பாசம் (pācam)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பாசம் (pācam) is borrowed from Sanskrit pāśa, \"a noose, a cord\" (CDIAL 8133): in Tamil, the tie of love that binds a family."
            }
          ]
        },
